; Regression test for GitHub issue #3314: each group of postings, the real
; ones and the balanced virtual ones in [brackets], may have one posting
; without an amount.  A transaction can therefore have two such postings,
; so when the balanced virtual postings have a second one, the error says
; which group it is in.
;
; A posting without an amount is zero when only the other group has
; amounts (see 3314_zero.test), but where no posting that must balance
; has one -- here the only amount is on a (parenthesized) virtual
; posting, which need not balance -- it has nothing to be computed from,
; as before.

2020-01-01 Groceries
    Expenses:Food                     $10.00
    Assets:Cash
    [Budget:Food]
    [Budget:Unallocated]

2020-01-02 Budget only
    (Budget:Food)                     $10.00
    Expenses:Food

test bal -> 2
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 17:
Error: Only one balanced virtual posting with null amount allowed per transaction
While parsing file "$FILE", line 21:
Error: There cannot be null amounts after balancing a transaction
end test
